update kb_entries set content = replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(content, $q$A project is **Completed** when all its work is finished, and **closed** when its WBS has been reviewed and its final numbers locked. Completed comes first; closing is the final sign-off. Click a section below to expand it.$q$, $q$Every project has one **Stage**. Finishing a project is one step: when every task is Done or Cancelled, the owner sends **Close Project** from the WBS page. While it waits the Stage is {orange:Closing}; once approved it's {success:Closed} (Completed), with Phase set to Done and the final numbers locked. Click a section below to expand it.

| Stage | What it means | How it gets there |
|---|---|---|
| {neutral:Draft} | Being planned. Tasks are private to the owner and their leaders. | New project |
| {gold:Awaiting Start} | A Start Project request is waiting for approval. | Owner sends **Start Project** (WBS page) |
| {accent:Active} | Started; the team is working on it. | Start Project approved, or Resume |
| {orange:Closing} | A Close Project request is waiting for approval. | Owner sends **Close Project** (all tasks Done or Cancelled) |
| {purple:Paused} | On hold. | **Pause** (reason required) |
| {success:Closed} | Finished. Final numbers are locked. | Close Project approved |
| {danger:Cancelled} | Stopped before it was finished. | **Cancel project** |$q$), $q$| | Project status **Completed** | WBS status **Closed** |
|---|---|---|
| What it means | All work is finished | Final numbers reviewed and locked |
| Who sets it | Project owner (manual) | Close Project request, routed to the first person up the owner's line with the Project Close right (or Full Access) |
| Tasks can be reopened | {success:Yes} — the project moves back to In Progress | {danger:No} — reopen the project through WBS first |
| Follow-up time allowed | {success:Yes} | {danger:No} |
| Existing logs can be corrected | {success:Yes} | {success:Yes} |$q$, $q$| | {accent:Active} · Ready to close | {success:Closed} |
|---|---|---|
| What it means | Every task is Done or Cancelled | Close Project approved; final numbers locked |
| Who sets it | Automatic tag | Close Project request, routed to the first person up the owner's line with the Project Close right (or Full Access) |
| Tasks can be reopened | {success:Yes} | {danger:No} — reopen the project through WBS first |
| Follow-up time allowed | {success:Yes} | {danger:No} |
| Existing logs can be corrected | {success:Yes} | {success:Yes} |$q$), $q$### Marking a project Completed
Project status is still set by hand, but Tempo checks the work first:

- A project can be set to **Completed** only when every task is **Done** or **Cancelled**.
- A project with **no tasks** can't be Completed or closed: no tasks means nothing happened. If work was done, add the tasks first; if not, **delete** the project (Tempo offers both options).
- If any task is still open, you'll see the list of open tasks (Task ID, name, status). **Finish** them, or **cancel** the ones that are no longer needed (with a reason) — then set the project to Completed.
- This matches **Actual Progress**: cancelled tasks don't count, so 100% means every remaining task is Done.
- If the whole project was stopped rather than finished, use **Cancelled** or **Paused**, not Completed.$q$, $q$### When a project is ready to close
There's no separate "mark Completed" step. Tempo checks the work for you:

- When every task is **Done** or **Cancelled**, the project shows {gold:Ready to close} next to its Stage.
- A project with **no tasks** can't be closed: no tasks means nothing happened. If work was done, add the tasks first; if not, move the project to Archive.
- If any task is still open, Close Project lists them. **Finish** them, or **cancel** the ones no longer needed (with a reason).
- If the whole project was stopped rather than finished, use **Cancel project** or **Pause** from the Stage cell, not Close Project.$q$), $q$### Reopening a task on a Completed project
If a task needs more work after the project was marked Completed, its Immediate Supervisor (or anyone above) can reopen it. Before it happens you'll see a warning, and then:

- the task goes back to **In Progress**, so Actual Progress drops below 100%;
- the project **automatically moves back to In Progress** (the phase moves to the latest In Progress phase);
- the project can only be set to Completed again once that task is Done or Cancelled.$q$, $q$### Reopening a task before closing
If a task needs more work while the project is still Active, its Immediate Supervisor (or anyone above) can reopen it. The task goes back to **In Progress**, so the {gold:Ready to close} tag goes away until it's Done or Cancelled again.$q$), $q$When a project is Completed, the owner reviews the WBS and requests closure from the WBS page.$q$, $q$When the project is Ready to close, the owner reviews the WBS and sends **Close Project** from the WBS page. Phase isn't needed: closing sets it to Done.$q$), $q$**Projects ready to close** lists Completed projects with how long ago they were completed and how many tasks still await validation, with a link to the WBS. **Completed projects have open tasks** flags any Completed project that has open work.$q$, $q$**Projects ready to close** lists your Active projects where every task is Done or Cancelled, with how long ago the last task was done and how many tasks still await validation, with a link to the WBS.$q$), $q$- **Projects & Tasks**: the WBS Status column shows a {gold:Ready to close} tag on Completed projects that aren't closed yet.$q$, $q$- **Projects & Tasks**: the Stage column shows a {gold:Ready to close} tag.$q$), $q$lists projects Completed **14+ days** ago that still aren't closed, so supervisors can follow up.$q$, $q$shows **Ready to close** (all done, no Close Project request yet) and **Closing** (request waiting), so supervisors can follow up.$q$), updated_by = 'e7e52a30-4c13-449b-889d-280dc0ca16c6', updated_at = now() where article_number = 6;
